### Leap Second Resolution Update
*   Kristof Teichel presented an update on the BIPM and ITU-R efforts to phase out leap seconds:
    *   In 2022, the BIPM decided to increase the leap second tolerance threshold beyond 1 second by 2035.
    *   In 2023, the ITU-R World Radio Conference proposed a new threshold of 1 hour (3,600 seconds).
    *   The BIPM General Conference of Weights and Measures (CGPM) is voting on this proposal between October 13 and 15, 2026. If accepted unanimously, it will take effect in May 2027, effectively ending the practice of introducing leap seconds for several thousand years.
    *   *Discussion*: Miroslav Lichvar asked if NTPv5 needs to deprecate leap seconds or support "leap hours." Kristof Teichel suggested keeping the protocol backward-compatible with NTPv4. Because a 1-hour deviation will take millennia to accumulate, the issue is functionally mitigated.

